# Gridiron VPS-1 host crontab fragment (runs as `deploy`).
#
# INSTALL (owner, on the box, after bootstrap + first deploy):
#   sudo cp scheduler/gridiron.cron /etc/cron.d/gridiron
#   sudo chmod 644 /etc/cron.d/gridiron
# (Cron.d requires a user column — included below — and absolute paths.)
#
# WHY HOST CRON, not a cron sidecar service (PLATFORM_SETUP §11):
# a sidecar would sit in RAM 24/7 on a 4 GB box just to sleep until Tuesday.
# Host cron is the single scheduler; silence is caught the same way either
# way — by the healthchecks.io dead-man pings each job sends on success
# (missing ping = page). One-shot services carry `restart: "no"` and
# `profiles: [jobs]`, so plain `up -d` never starts them.
#
# TZ note: cron runs these in the host timezone — keep the box on UTC
# (bootstrap.sh forces UTC) so "Tue 13:00" means 13:00 UTC, today's ETL slot.
# ETL and backup windows do not overlap (Tue 13:00 vs daily 03:30), so the
# 1.5 GB ETL and 512 MB backup budgets never stack on top of serving.

SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
COMPOSE_DIR=/srv/gridiron

# Weekly refresh: Tuesday 13:00 UTC (today's standing slot).
0 13 * * 2 deploy cd /srv/gridiron && /usr/bin/docker compose --profile jobs run --rm etl >>/var/log/gridiron-etl.log 2>&1

# Nightly R2 backup: daily 03:30 UTC.
30 3 * * * deploy cd /srv/gridiron && /usr/bin/docker compose --profile jobs run --rm backup >>/var/log/gridiron-backup.log 2>&1
